..
  Create a fragment with: west release-fragment new
  or copy this file to doc/releases/draft/fragments/<descriptive-name>.rst and fill it in.

  ::area:: must name an area in MAINTAINERS.yml, or "Tree-wide changes" for a change that affects
  applications across the tree.
  ::pr:: is the number of the pull request that adds this fragment; list several separated by
  commas when the change spans more than one.
  Write one fragment per change. A change with several points gets one fragment with a short
  lead sentence and a list, not one fragment per point.
  Fill in ::release-notes::, ::migration-guide:: or both, and delete the one you do not need. Each
  feeds the document of the same name, and the generated entries link to each other, so describe
  the capability in one and the required action in the other instead of repeating it.

  The security notice is not built from fragments: the security team curates it in
  doc/releases/draft/security-notice.rst.inc.

  Markers start at column 0 and their content runs until the next marker. Content is regular
  reStructuredText: paragraphs, lists and code-block directives are all allowed, section
  headings are not.

  Validate with: scripts/release/release_fragments.py check

::area:: Component
::pr:: 12345

::release-notes::
.. What changed and why it matters to users.

::migration-guide::
.. What an application must change, and what to use instead of anything deprecated or removed.
